{"artifact_id":"extract_c5bf2c716bc7011f18bfb542","byte_end":64923,"byte_start":61025,"format_id":"reviewed-html-paragraph-v1","locator":"Ch0.S3.p8.1","original_html":"<p id=\"Ch0.S3.p8.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">Sphaleron production depends on two parameters, <math id=\"Ch0.S3.p8.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"E_{\\text{sph}}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mtext>sph</mtext></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_{\\text{sph}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id=\"Ch0.S3.p8.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"N_{\\text{CS}}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>CS</mtext></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N_{\\text{CS}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The parameter <math id=\"Ch0.S3.p8.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"E_{\\text{sph}}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mtext>sph</mtext></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_{\\text{sph}}</annotation></semantics></math> is scanned in a range from 8.5 to 9.5<span id=\"Ch0.S3.p8.1.1\" class=\"ltx_ERROR undefined\">\\TeV</span>in steps of 0.25<span id=\"Ch0.S3.p8.1.2\" class=\"ltx_ERROR undefined\">\\TeV</span>.\nSince the sphaleron transition is exponentially suppressed by <math id=\"Ch0.S3.p8.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\abs{N_{\\text{CS}}}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mtext class=\"undefined\">\\abs</mtext><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">\u200b</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>CS</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\abs{N_{\\text{CS}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, only <math id=\"Ch0.S3.p8.m5\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"N_{\\text{CS}}=\\pm 1\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>CS</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>\u00b1</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N_{\\text{CS}}=\\pm 1</annotation></semantics></math> are simulated. The probability of <math id=\"Ch0.S3.p8.m6\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"N_{\\text{CS}}=+1\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>CS</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N_{\\text{CS}}=+1</annotation></semantics></math> is denoted as <math id=\"Ch0.S3.p8.m7\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"p({N_{\\text{CS}}})\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>\u2061</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>CS</mtext></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p({N_{\\text{CS}}})</annotation></semantics></math>. The <math id=\"Ch0.S3.p8.m8\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"p({N_{\\text{CS}}})\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>\u2061</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>CS</mtext></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p({N_{\\text{CS}}})</annotation></semantics></math> values of 0%, 50%, and 100% were used, where, for example, <math id=\"Ch0.S3.p8.m9\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"p({N_{\\text{CS}}})=50\\%\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>\u2061</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>CS</mtext></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p({N_{\\text{CS}}})=50\\%</annotation></semantics></math> means half of the events have <math id=\"Ch0.S3.p8.m10\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"N_{\\text{CS}}=+1\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>CS</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N_{\\text{CS}}=+1</annotation></semantics></math> and half have <math id=\"Ch0.S3.p8.m11\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"N_{\\text{CS}}=-1\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>CS</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>\u2212</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N_{\\text{CS}}=-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>","parser_version":"1.0.0","purpose":"RESEARCH","review_status":"PROPOSED","schema_version":"1.0.0","source_hash":"7fadcfce5fce60055ccd817d98d05c9d09e4c759f1691022a0d3f4f7cf2be955","source_id":"cms_paper_v2","source_version":"2604.10732v2"}